1
00:00:00,039 --> 00:00:01,455
(This drama complied with production
guidelines for filming child actors,)

2
00:00:01,458 --> 00:00:03,000
(and some scenes used
generative AI technology.)

3
00:00:04,405 --> 00:00:06,622
What could she have learned from her mom?

4
00:00:07,328 --> 00:00:09,995
She probably used her looks
to seduce men...

5
00:00:10,036 --> 00:00:13,745
and pretended to be an artist
just because she could paint a little.

6
00:00:14,245 --> 00:00:15,870
A genius? Hardly.

7
00:00:16,120 --> 00:00:17,495
I know exactly what happened.

8
00:00:18,328 --> 00:00:20,995
Mother, I feel so much better.

9
00:00:21,036 --> 00:00:22,786
You're no ordinary person.

10
00:00:23,036 --> 00:00:26,193
How dare she lay a hand on you?
You're my daughter-in-law.

11
00:00:26,995 --> 00:00:28,328
It's so frustrating.

12
00:00:34,495 --> 00:00:36,286
- Does it hurt?
- It hurts so bad.

13
00:00:37,870 --> 00:00:40,731
You must've been really scared.
Your pulse is racing.

14
00:00:41,578 --> 00:00:42,578
Really?

15
00:00:43,911 --> 00:00:47,578
No, you're fine. It's not that bad.

16
00:00:47,661 --> 00:00:49,661
Come on, Sa Bin!

17
00:00:49,745 --> 00:00:51,911
She's tough, so she's okay for now.

18
00:00:52,245 --> 00:00:54,953
Who could be okay
after getting beaten like that?

19
00:00:55,383 --> 00:00:56,758
Please take good care of her.

20
00:00:57,216 --> 00:00:58,883
Her mom is overseas too.

21
00:00:59,203 --> 00:01:01,078
I guess I'll have to be her mom now.

22
00:01:01,245 --> 00:01:03,828
Mother, I'm so touched.

23
00:01:03,953 --> 00:01:05,411
You really are so kindhearted.

24
00:01:05,453 --> 00:01:07,578
My mom is really scary.

25
00:01:07,620 --> 00:01:09,453
I've never heard her
say anything like that.

26
00:01:09,495 --> 00:01:11,828
Your mom can be a little cold.

27
00:01:12,036 --> 00:01:14,953
Still, she absolutely adores you.

28
00:01:15,495 --> 00:01:17,828
Anyone would think
you were raised by a stepmother.

29
00:01:17,870 --> 00:01:20,453
I really thought I'd been adopted
when I was little.

30
00:01:21,495 --> 00:01:23,008
Big baby, let's go to the treatment room.

31
00:01:23,370 --> 00:01:25,203
I'll give you some acupuncture
to calm you down.

32
00:01:25,245 --> 00:01:26,370
It won't hurt, right?

33
00:01:26,411 --> 00:01:28,353
You have to tough it out.

34
00:01:29,036 --> 00:01:30,745
It'll hurt a lot.

35
00:01:30,786 --> 00:01:32,245
What do we do? This is bad. Let's go.

36
00:01:32,328 --> 00:01:34,118
- Please be gentle.
- Mother, I don't like needles.

37
00:01:34,120 --> 00:01:35,870
Come on, let's go.

38
00:01:38,911 --> 00:01:41,495
She's such a scaredy-cat.

39
00:01:49,411 --> 00:01:50,703
Just wait here a moment.

40
00:01:55,722 --> 00:01:56,972
Are you here?

41
00:02:03,620 --> 00:02:04,911
Maestro, you're here?

42
00:02:05,120 --> 00:02:07,411
Yeah. It's my wrist.

43
00:02:14,245 --> 00:02:15,911
- Who?
- She's my sister-in-law.

44
00:02:15,953 --> 00:02:19,409
For a second,
I thought she was the third woman.

45
00:02:19,412 --> 00:02:20,436
What?

46
00:02:20,469 --> 00:02:22,036
I'm not that much of a ladies' man.

47
00:02:22,161 --> 00:02:23,161
Have a seat.

48
00:02:26,620 --> 00:02:28,120
What did the doctor say?

49
00:02:28,161 --> 00:02:29,786
He said it's dystonia.

50
00:02:29,870 --> 00:02:31,536
It's common among musicians.

51
00:02:31,578 --> 00:02:33,161
I know.

52
00:02:33,703 --> 00:02:35,953
- He gave you a prescription, right?
- Yeah.

53
00:02:35,995 --> 00:02:37,453
I'll make you some herbal medicine too.

54
00:02:37,578 --> 00:02:39,245
Sa Bin.

55
00:02:40,328 --> 00:02:43,036
Actually, I came to ask you a favor.

56
00:02:43,328 --> 00:02:46,745
Could I borrow that money
we talked about before?

57
00:02:46,786 --> 00:02:50,781
I'm sorry, but I don't think I can.

58
00:02:51,703 --> 00:02:53,161
- Did you spend it?
- No.

59
00:02:53,995 --> 00:02:55,590
I think I'll need it.

60
00:02:56,203 --> 00:02:57,536
Yeong Ju?

61
00:02:59,786 --> 00:03:01,585
Sa Bin, we're leaving.

62
00:03:01,953 --> 00:03:02,995
Goodbye...

63
00:03:04,078 --> 00:03:05,120
Ma'am?

64
00:03:05,370 --> 00:03:06,370
"Ma'am?"

65
00:03:07,620 --> 00:03:09,286
That's her. The thug's mom.

66
00:03:09,536 --> 00:03:11,328
That mistress...

67
00:03:11,578 --> 00:03:12,786
Seriously!

68
00:03:13,411 --> 00:03:14,578
Listen.

69
00:03:15,161 --> 00:03:17,161
You should've raised your daughter better.

70
00:03:17,286 --> 00:03:19,411
Even if you lived however you wanted,

71
00:03:19,870 --> 00:03:22,578
you should've at least taught
your daughter better.

72
00:03:22,911 --> 00:03:26,370
Unbelievable. What are you saying?

73
00:03:26,495 --> 00:03:28,953
How dare you call
someone else's daughter a thug?

74
00:03:29,411 --> 00:03:30,703
Come here.

75
00:03:31,620 --> 00:03:35,284
She did this to her.
What else would I call her?

76
00:03:35,286 --> 00:03:36,870
Did Ji Ni hit you?

77
00:03:36,911 --> 00:03:38,993
Yeah. She kicked me
and twisted my wrist...

78
00:03:38,995 --> 00:03:40,536
What about Ji Ni?

79
00:03:40,995 --> 00:03:42,661
She must be hurt too.

80
00:03:43,245 --> 00:03:45,078
Look at you,
worrying about your own daughter.

81
00:03:45,328 --> 00:03:46,512
Look at this.

82
00:03:47,161 --> 00:03:50,120
When you meet the victim,
you should apologize first.

83
00:03:50,203 --> 00:03:52,076
Sun Kyung, all of a sudden...

84
00:03:52,078 --> 00:03:54,411
Is this woman the maestro
you said you admired?

85
00:03:54,453 --> 00:03:55,453
"This woman?"

86
00:03:55,703 --> 00:03:56,784
Look here.

87
00:03:56,786 --> 00:04:00,036
Do you know what kind of woman she is?
And you admire her as a maestro?

88
00:04:00,120 --> 00:04:01,661
Sa Bin.

89
00:04:02,203 --> 00:04:05,911
She's a criminal who wrecked a family.

90
00:04:06,036 --> 00:04:07,978
If your brother finds out, he'll faint.

91
00:04:11,911 --> 00:04:14,248
Sun Kyung, I'll handle this.

92
00:04:14,536 --> 00:04:15,870
Do Hee, take her out.

93
00:04:16,536 --> 00:04:17,604
Seriously!

94
00:04:21,286 --> 00:04:24,661
Mother, you avoid shit because it's dirty,

95
00:04:24,745 --> 00:04:25,786
not because you're scared of it.

96
00:04:25,911 --> 00:04:26,953
You little...

97
00:04:27,120 --> 00:04:28,120
Do Hee!

98
00:04:35,745 --> 00:04:37,442
Seriously, I...

99
00:04:38,911 --> 00:04:40,565
I'm sorry.

100
00:04:40,703 --> 00:04:41,887
Please, just bear with her.

101
00:04:42,078 --> 00:04:43,909
I think she's misunderstood something.

102
00:04:43,911 --> 00:04:45,745
I'll explain everything tonight.

103
00:04:46,328 --> 00:04:47,485
Seriously!

104
00:04:47,828 --> 00:04:50,828
How long do I have to keep talking
about what happened 30 years ago?

105
00:04:51,495 --> 00:04:52,495
Maestro.

106
00:04:52,558 --> 00:04:54,856
Why did you show up only now?

107
00:04:54,911 --> 00:04:56,828
If you'd married Yeong Ju sooner,

108
00:04:56,953 --> 00:04:59,828
I could've done the paperwork sooner,
and she would've been happy.

109
00:04:59,870 --> 00:05:02,120
Then my daughter and I
wouldn't have had to hear all this.

110
00:05:03,411 --> 00:05:04,451
I know.

111
00:05:04,453 --> 00:05:05,703
Seriously!

112
00:05:06,828 --> 00:05:10,745
I know I was wrong too,
but I'm so sick of Yeong Ju.

113
00:05:12,078 --> 00:05:15,222
I'm sorry. That's honestly how I feel.

114
00:05:15,620 --> 00:05:17,001
It is what it is.

115
00:05:17,620 --> 00:05:18,745
See you later.

116
00:05:46,245 --> 00:05:47,976
Why do you keep coming
to someone else's workplace?

117
00:05:48,036 --> 00:05:49,036
"Someone else?"

118
00:05:49,756 --> 00:05:52,188
Like I'm a stranger. You brat!

119
00:05:52,786 --> 00:05:53,945
I heard you two fought.

120
00:05:54,036 --> 00:05:55,055
You're not hurt, right?

121
00:05:55,058 --> 00:05:56,244
How did you know?

122
00:05:57,078 --> 00:05:58,284
Did you see Do Hee?

123
00:05:58,286 --> 00:05:59,837
I saw her at the Oriental Medicine Clinic.

124
00:05:59,995 --> 00:06:03,120
The woman with her, who looked like
her mother-in-law, called you a thug.

125
00:06:04,536 --> 00:06:06,067
I heard it when I confronted her about it.

126
00:06:07,370 --> 00:06:08,859
Are you really not hurt?

127
00:06:09,036 --> 00:06:10,411
Tell me if you're in pain.

128
00:06:10,495 --> 00:06:12,411
She was there for acupuncture
and medicine.

129
00:06:12,578 --> 00:06:14,995
You're already frail.
Don't wear yourself out.

130
00:06:15,078 --> 00:06:16,168
I'm fine.

131
00:06:16,620 --> 00:06:17,620
Go.

132
00:06:18,328 --> 00:06:20,659
Your dad shouldn't have taught you
how to fight.

133
00:06:20,661 --> 00:06:22,004
I never liked that.

134
00:06:23,953 --> 00:06:25,236
Here. A pain patch.

135
00:06:26,745 --> 00:06:27,745
I'm going.

136
00:06:28,161 --> 00:06:29,161
Okay.

137
00:06:32,536 --> 00:06:33,641
You...

138
00:06:35,245 --> 00:06:36,661
Are you really not getting married?

139
00:06:36,703 --> 00:06:38,953
No one's asked me to marry them.

140
00:06:39,155 --> 00:06:41,018
- Would you if someone did?
- Mom.

141
00:06:42,536 --> 00:06:45,216
You should get married soon
and make it official.

142
00:06:45,219 --> 00:06:46,826
Aren't you sick
of being treated like this?

143
00:06:46,828 --> 00:06:48,931
It's fine. I'm okay.

144
00:06:51,536 --> 00:06:52,536
I'm going.

145
00:07:16,995 --> 00:07:18,245
Ji Ni, it's me.

146
00:07:18,578 --> 00:07:20,124
You need to eat.

147
00:07:21,247 --> 00:07:22,891
Are you really going to starve yourself?

148
00:07:22,953 --> 00:07:25,495
Should we all just die, then?

149
00:07:25,578 --> 00:07:26,620
Ji Ni.

150
00:07:29,495 --> 00:07:30,909
I won't eat food from a mistress.

151
00:07:30,911 --> 00:07:32,786
Ji Ni, don't say things like that.

152
00:07:33,786 --> 00:07:34,953
Cheater.

153
00:07:36,495 --> 00:07:38,726
You're right. I'm a cheater.

154
00:07:38,828 --> 00:07:40,120
I'm sorry. I was wrong.

155
00:07:40,328 --> 00:07:42,948
I should've done better
to protect you and your mom.

156
00:07:43,953 --> 00:07:45,286
It's my fault.

157
00:07:45,620 --> 00:07:46,817
Liar.

158
00:07:50,078 --> 00:07:51,161
Mistress.

159
00:07:52,578 --> 00:07:55,036
Your mom and I love you so much.

160
00:07:55,078 --> 00:07:56,925
I wronged that family, but...

161
00:07:57,661 --> 00:07:59,747
I didn't want to hurt you or your mom,

162
00:07:59,995 --> 00:08:01,480
so I made a choice.

163
00:08:08,703 --> 00:08:09,881
I'm sorry.

164
00:08:10,661 --> 00:08:14,492
I'm so sorry I made you feel ashamed.

165
00:08:14,495 --> 00:08:15,898
What's wrong with you?

166
00:08:16,245 --> 00:08:18,953
Why are you kneeling
in front of her? Get up.

167
00:08:19,286 --> 00:08:20,370
Get up.

168
00:08:20,911 --> 00:08:22,703
This all happened because of who?

169
00:08:23,036 --> 00:08:25,203
I did this because I couldn't give you up.

170
00:08:31,370 --> 00:08:32,910
I shouldn't have been born.

171
00:08:34,786 --> 00:08:36,120
I'm a child of sin.

172
00:08:38,578 --> 00:08:39,896
No.

173
00:08:40,828 --> 00:08:42,307
No, don't blame yourself.

174
00:08:43,036 --> 00:08:44,953
You did nothing wrong. It's all my fault.

175
00:08:45,078 --> 00:08:46,286
Blame me.

176
00:08:46,328 --> 00:08:48,477
Your mom did nothing wrong either.
It's all my fault.

177
00:08:53,620 --> 00:08:55,721
You're the result of your parents' love.

178
00:08:56,078 --> 00:08:57,328
So never...

179
00:08:58,995 --> 00:09:00,320
Never again...

180
00:09:01,995 --> 00:09:03,578
have thoughts like that.

181
00:09:23,286 --> 00:09:25,275
Ji Ni!

182
00:09:26,745 --> 00:09:28,370
Calm down. Are you okay?

183
00:09:33,536 --> 00:09:35,870
You little brat,
you're going to be the death of me.

184
00:09:45,661 --> 00:09:48,121
If you die, I'll die too.

185
00:09:51,495 --> 00:09:53,043
I hate you the most.

186
00:09:54,411 --> 00:09:56,195
Hate me, resent me, do whatever you want.

187
00:09:56,245 --> 00:09:57,939
But you can't die.

188
00:09:58,620 --> 00:10:00,245
Sit properly and eat, you brat.

189
00:10:01,078 --> 00:10:03,870
Why are you letting her intimidate you?

190
00:10:05,120 --> 00:10:08,630
Even if the whole world blames him,
you can't.

191
00:10:08,870 --> 00:10:11,193
Your dad always did right by you.

192
00:10:12,161 --> 00:10:14,578
Why can't you see that?
Why won't you see it?

193
00:10:15,370 --> 00:10:18,328
He did it all to protect
the three of us...

194
00:11:26,822 --> 00:11:28,797
What's this?

195
00:11:28,911 --> 00:11:30,187
Did you buy clothes?

196
00:11:30,786 --> 00:11:31,995
I bought them for her.

197
00:11:32,120 --> 00:11:34,245
So that's why you asked this morning?

198
00:11:34,286 --> 00:11:37,225
I went to buy maternity clothes
and we shopped together.

199
00:11:37,536 --> 00:11:38,771
Mine look pretty too, right?

200
00:11:39,620 --> 00:11:41,160
We have different body types.

201
00:11:41,162 --> 00:11:43,453
Just because we dress alike
doesn't mean our style's the same.

202
00:11:44,104 --> 00:11:46,243
Second Mother.

203
00:11:46,245 --> 00:11:47,245
You...

204
00:11:47,622 --> 00:11:49,955
I can't call you "Teacher."

205
00:11:50,036 --> 00:11:52,534
Then what, am I supposed
to call you "Maestro" at home?

206
00:11:52,536 --> 00:11:54,828
Fine. Do whatever you want.

207
00:11:54,953 --> 00:11:57,286
I'm so sick of this "second" nonsense.

208
00:12:19,786 --> 00:12:21,864
What? Did you break the cup?

209
00:12:26,036 --> 00:12:28,252
Are your hands shaking?

210
00:12:28,286 --> 00:12:29,536
You're a musician...

211
00:12:29,620 --> 00:12:32,050
I'm just low on energy.

212
00:12:33,411 --> 00:12:34,819
It's because of you.

213
00:12:39,703 --> 00:12:41,893
You really have an excuse for everything.

214
00:13:18,245 --> 00:13:20,997
Se Ri, what's wrong?

215
00:13:21,911 --> 00:13:24,870
Go away.

216
00:13:25,536 --> 00:13:28,661
I don't want to see anyone.

217
00:14:14,286 --> 00:14:15,454
Mother.

218
00:14:15,995 --> 00:14:18,620
You said you had plans. Go.

219
00:14:19,995 --> 00:14:22,716
Once my second mother calms down
and comes out,

220
00:14:23,161 --> 00:14:24,427
I'll take care of her.

221
00:14:30,988 --> 00:14:32,291
O Reum's getting a sibling?

222
00:14:32,988 --> 00:14:33,988
Yeah.

223
00:14:35,321 --> 00:14:36,535
Aren't you going to congratulate me?

224
00:14:37,529 --> 00:14:40,529
Of course I am. But...

225
00:14:41,446 --> 00:14:42,462
But what?

226
00:14:43,237 --> 00:14:45,987
You're already pushing me away
because you're a grandmother.

227
00:14:46,404 --> 00:14:50,101
I'm worried you'll push me away even more.

228
00:14:51,538 --> 00:14:52,746
You're right.

229
00:14:53,321 --> 00:14:55,654
I've been reminded of my place again.

230
00:14:56,904 --> 00:14:57,990
Yeong Ju,

231
00:14:57,992 --> 00:15:00,783
Being a grandmother is your family role,

232
00:15:00,804 --> 00:15:03,116
not proof that you're no longer a woman.

233
00:15:03,779 --> 00:15:04,843
I know.

234
00:15:05,970 --> 00:15:06,980
But...

235
00:15:07,465 --> 00:15:10,804
I found out Se Ri
was the musician you admired,

236
00:15:11,321 --> 00:15:12,718
and it hit me again.

237
00:15:13,654 --> 00:15:15,043
As a woman,

238
00:15:16,029 --> 00:15:17,614
I've really had bad luck.

239
00:15:18,529 --> 00:15:19,694
And it had to be Se Ri.

240
00:15:19,696 --> 00:15:21,777
You really don't have to worry about that.

241
00:15:21,779 --> 00:15:25,113
I guess I'm only lucky
when it comes to family.

242
00:15:25,946 --> 00:15:28,320
My in-laws were wonderful too.

243
00:15:29,196 --> 00:15:31,899
My mother-in-law got
on my nerves sometimes.

244
00:15:32,696 --> 00:15:35,778
But I truly respected my father-in-law.

245
00:15:36,354 --> 00:15:40,060
My two sons and daughter-in-law
are all good people too.

246
00:15:40,613 --> 00:15:41,613
What about me?

247
00:15:42,904 --> 00:15:44,071
Sa Bin.

248
00:15:45,238 --> 00:15:47,196
Is there really no place for me?

249
00:15:48,029 --> 00:15:51,529
I think I'll quit the singing class
for a while.

250
00:15:52,446 --> 00:15:54,404
With Mai taking care of O Reum,

251
00:15:54,529 --> 00:15:56,760
it'll be hard for her
to raise another child.

252
00:15:57,404 --> 00:15:58,613
I'll do it.

253
00:15:59,029 --> 00:16:00,881
I'm still fit as a fiddle.

254
00:16:12,865 --> 00:16:14,252
Congratulations!

255
00:16:14,254 --> 00:16:15,462
I'm happier than you are.

256
00:16:15,571 --> 00:16:16,571
Mai!

257
00:16:17,528 --> 00:16:18,528
Congratulations!

258
00:16:21,738 --> 00:16:23,361
Cake cutting!

259
00:16:23,363 --> 00:16:26,154
Cut the cake together.

260
00:16:27,613 --> 00:16:30,042
Thank you.

261
00:16:30,071 --> 00:16:32,862
- Congratulations.
- Congratulations!

262
00:16:34,512 --> 00:16:37,706
O Reum, let's go outside too.

263
00:16:38,988 --> 00:16:41,202
You'll have a little sibling now.

264
00:16:43,979 --> 00:16:45,527
Get up.

265
00:16:48,154 --> 00:16:50,446
Mai, say a few words.

266
00:16:52,238 --> 00:16:55,238
Thank you, everyone.

267
00:16:56,946 --> 00:16:59,194
We'll make sure our second child is born
healthy and strong,

268
00:16:59,196 --> 00:17:01,035
and raise them to be as strong as O Reum,

269
00:17:01,196 --> 00:17:06,113
a healthy Korean-Vietnamese child.

270
00:17:09,020 --> 00:17:11,935
I'm jealous.
When will I have grandchildren?

271
00:17:11,946 --> 00:17:14,238
You need to say it louder.
Can she hear you like that?

272
00:17:14,279 --> 00:17:16,985
Your mom says she wants grandchildren.

273
00:17:16,988 --> 00:17:18,069
Na Ji Ni!

274
00:17:18,072 --> 00:17:20,780
You too. Why are you yelling
at someone else?

275
00:17:21,113 --> 00:17:22,331
You too.

276
00:17:23,946 --> 00:17:26,529
Ji Ni, come out.

277
00:17:26,821 --> 00:17:28,904
If you can't wake O Reum, just come out.

278
00:17:33,238 --> 00:17:34,333
Listen...

279
00:17:35,404 --> 00:17:38,321
I think O Reum has a fever.

280
00:17:38,912 --> 00:17:39,912
What?

281
00:17:47,196 --> 00:17:49,236
Seung Woo, call 911.

282
00:17:49,238 --> 00:17:51,029
- Hurry!
- Okay.

283
00:17:51,363 --> 00:17:53,446
- O Reum, wake up.
- Yes, 911?

284
00:17:53,654 --> 00:17:54,863
O Reum.

285
00:17:55,522 --> 00:17:56,528
Bring cold water.

286
00:17:56,531 --> 00:17:58,696
- O Reum, wake up.
- O Reum.

287
00:17:58,988 --> 00:18:00,944
- O Reum.
- He's unconscious.

288
00:18:00,946 --> 00:18:02,361
I think he's having trouble breathing.

289
00:18:02,363 --> 00:18:03,585
O Reum.

290
00:18:04,529 --> 00:18:07,946
- O Reum.
- O Reum.

291
00:18:09,363 --> 00:18:11,568
- O Reum, wake up.
- O Reum.

292
00:18:15,446 --> 00:18:17,988
(Haemyeong University Hospital)

293
00:18:18,404 --> 00:18:20,466
- We'll take him to the examination room.
- Okay.

294
00:18:20,662 --> 00:18:23,049
O Reum.

295
00:18:28,196 --> 00:18:29,988
- You two stay here.
- O Reum.

296
00:18:30,446 --> 00:18:31,654
O Reum.

297
00:18:33,279 --> 00:18:35,363
- What should we do?
- Mom.

298
00:18:37,196 --> 00:18:40,279
It's okay.

299
00:18:45,821 --> 00:18:46,988
Carry these.

300
00:18:50,096 --> 00:18:51,096
Go.

301
00:19:09,613 --> 00:19:11,141
Leave it.

302
00:19:11,238 --> 00:19:12,988
Why are you doing that?

303
00:19:13,378 --> 00:19:14,628
I'm good at it.

304
00:19:14,738 --> 00:19:16,738
I've been washing dishes
at a cafe for years.

305
00:19:16,863 --> 00:19:18,779
That's just a part-time job.

306
00:19:19,071 --> 00:19:21,319
You can't seriously wash dishes here.

307
00:19:21,322 --> 00:19:22,555
Go carry the plates.

308
00:19:22,571 --> 00:19:24,569
And put the leftovers in the fridge.

309
00:19:24,571 --> 00:19:27,238
What's the big deal? Why can't I do it?

310
00:19:27,363 --> 00:19:29,488
Didn't you bring me here to live?

311
00:19:29,529 --> 00:19:32,988
It's already strange that you and I
are living here together,

312
00:19:33,029 --> 00:19:34,738
but now you're even washing dishes?

313
00:19:35,946 --> 00:19:37,488
This might give me nightmares.

314
00:19:42,946 --> 00:19:45,529
Mom, O Reum will be okay, right?

315
00:19:46,363 --> 00:19:47,735
He'll be fine.

316
00:19:47,738 --> 00:19:50,444
But someone else's marrow can't...

317
00:19:50,446 --> 00:19:52,279
take hold as quickly as his own would.

318
00:19:52,321 --> 00:19:54,321
It may take time, but it will settle in.

319
00:19:54,988 --> 00:19:58,279
Many transplant patients
live well. Don't worry.

320
00:19:58,571 --> 00:20:00,633
I really hope so.

321
00:20:01,426 --> 00:20:03,611
Mom, should I go to the hospital?

322
00:20:03,613 --> 00:20:05,486
His family's already there.
Why should you go too?

323
00:20:05,488 --> 00:20:08,113
Don't take it too far.

324
00:20:08,446 --> 00:20:12,321
Remember, they're just people we met
because we had no choice.

325
00:20:34,870 --> 00:20:35,946
What did they say?

326
00:20:36,488 --> 00:20:39,446
His breathing is stable now, but...

327
00:20:39,904 --> 00:20:41,527
after the stem cell transplant,

328
00:20:41,529 --> 00:20:43,808
his immune system hasn't fully recovered,

329
00:20:44,529 --> 00:20:46,279
so they suspect an infection.

330
00:20:47,946 --> 00:20:49,633
We knew this could happen.

331
00:20:50,312 --> 00:20:52,120
He was doing so well lately.

332
00:20:53,154 --> 00:20:54,738
Mom.

333
00:20:55,154 --> 00:20:58,014
O Reum, are you awake?

334
00:20:58,821 --> 00:21:00,745
It's Grandma. Do you recognize me?

335
00:21:03,238 --> 00:21:04,986
Hospital again?

336
00:21:05,126 --> 00:21:08,111
O Reum, you had a high fever.

337
00:21:08,251 --> 00:21:09,444
That's why you're here.

338
00:21:09,446 --> 00:21:12,277
I hate hospitals. Let's go home.

339
00:21:12,279 --> 00:21:13,349
O Reum.

340
00:21:14,026 --> 00:21:17,420
O Reum, you wanted to be brave
like me, remember?

341
00:21:19,238 --> 00:21:20,444
Let's stay here for today.

342
00:21:20,446 --> 00:21:22,113
With your mom and me. Okay?

343
00:21:23,154 --> 00:21:24,946
Okay.

344
00:21:25,613 --> 00:21:26,972
My sweet boy.

345
00:21:27,404 --> 00:21:29,196
Let's rest a little more.

346
00:21:32,988 --> 00:21:34,801
Mom, go home.

347
00:21:35,863 --> 00:21:38,569
Seung Woo, take Mai home.

348
00:21:38,571 --> 00:21:41,708
I'll stay with Seung Hyun tonight.

349
00:21:43,821 --> 00:21:45,614
Yes. You go home, honey.

350
00:21:51,229 --> 00:21:52,816
I need to stay by his side.

351
00:21:52,988 --> 00:21:54,321
Mother, you go home.

352
00:21:54,946 --> 00:21:56,238
I'll stay tonight.

353
00:21:56,321 --> 00:21:57,783
Go home, get some sleep, and come back.

354
00:21:58,321 --> 00:21:59,402
Right, Mai.

355
00:21:59,404 --> 00:22:01,743
You're pregnant. Come home with me.

356
00:22:08,471 --> 00:22:09,662
I'm worried.

357
00:22:10,238 --> 00:22:11,672
He'll be okay, right?

358
00:22:12,946 --> 00:22:15,363
He'll be fine. He's survived worse.

359
00:22:15,366 --> 00:22:16,954
We have to have faith.

360
00:22:37,821 --> 00:22:39,097
How is he?

361
00:22:39,488 --> 00:22:40,904
He's stable for now.

362
00:22:41,079 --> 00:22:43,014
We'll talk to the doctor tomorrow.

363
00:22:47,321 --> 00:22:49,439
Would you like some warm plum tea?

364
00:22:54,495 --> 00:22:55,703
Rest for now.

365
00:22:55,904 --> 00:22:57,143
We'll go early tomorrow.

366
00:22:57,696 --> 00:23:00,041
Okay. Thanks.

367
00:23:01,404 --> 00:23:02,495
It's nothing.

368
00:23:09,904 --> 00:23:11,349
Drink it slowly.

369
00:23:15,488 --> 00:23:17,108
- Isn't it too hot?
- No.

370
00:23:21,321 --> 00:23:22,372
What did you say?

371
00:23:22,738 --> 00:23:24,431
I met her myself.

372
00:23:25,004 --> 00:23:28,520
I called her a mistress,
and she couldn't say a word.

373
00:23:28,696 --> 00:23:30,196
So it must be true.

374
00:23:30,495 --> 00:23:32,402
Would she have stayed quiet if it wasn't?

375
00:23:32,404 --> 00:23:33,738
That's a serious accusation.

376
00:23:33,988 --> 00:23:35,444
Are you sure it was Ji Ni's mother?

377
00:23:35,446 --> 00:23:37,654
Yes. How many times do I have to say it?

378
00:23:38,154 --> 00:23:40,113
Do you think I'm making this up?

379
00:23:41,196 --> 00:23:42,779
Don't trust her too much.

380
00:23:42,946 --> 00:23:44,946
That's how children are raised.

381
00:23:44,988 --> 00:23:46,863
They learn from what they see at home.

382
00:23:47,146 --> 00:23:48,355
Her father...

383
00:23:48,404 --> 00:23:50,738
They say he adored his daughter,

384
00:23:50,863 --> 00:23:54,154
but abandoning his two sons
must have devastated them.

385
00:23:56,821 --> 00:23:59,251
They were suddenly left with one parent,

386
00:24:00,037 --> 00:24:02,996
while their father doted on the daughter
he had with his mistress.

387
00:24:03,488 --> 00:24:05,520
I feel terrible for those sons.

388
00:24:08,204 --> 00:24:10,376
Fire her when you get the chance.

389
00:24:11,093 --> 00:24:12,694
Aren't we lucky Ji Hu is dating...

390
00:24:12,696 --> 00:24:15,537
a girl from a respectable family
instead of someone like her?

391
00:24:17,904 --> 00:24:19,821
- Honey.
- Yes? What?

392
00:24:20,029 --> 00:24:22,154
Why are you ignoring what I said?

393
00:24:22,696 --> 00:24:24,861
You haven't said a word.

394
00:24:24,863 --> 00:24:26,736
It's just a lot to take in.

395
00:24:26,738 --> 00:24:28,444
What's so shocking about it?

396
00:24:28,446 --> 00:24:30,819
Mistresses are everywhere.

397
00:24:30,821 --> 00:24:34,071
There are so many.
Most just pretend they aren't.

398
00:24:34,196 --> 00:24:35,486
Well, that's true.

399
00:24:35,488 --> 00:24:37,726
They may call it love or whatever, but...

400
00:24:37,821 --> 00:24:40,404
people, especially adults,

401
00:24:40,529 --> 00:24:44,236
must never act unreasonably,
no matter the circumstances.

402
00:24:44,329 --> 00:24:45,833
- Don't you agree?
- Of course.

403
00:24:47,954 --> 00:24:49,547
So your conscience is clear?

404
00:24:50,078 --> 00:24:51,097
Of course.

405
00:24:51,722 --> 00:24:53,736
I just hope our future in-law...

406
00:24:53,738 --> 00:24:56,069
keeps promises and acts reasonably,

407
00:24:56,071 --> 00:24:58,260
with nothing to be ashamed of.

408
00:24:59,046 --> 00:25:00,671
That's basic decency.

409
00:25:01,988 --> 00:25:04,613
- Well, then.
- One more thing.

410
00:25:04,771 --> 00:25:05,979
A very important thing.

411
00:25:07,570 --> 00:25:09,560
- Sa Bin.
- What about him now?

412
00:25:13,488 --> 00:25:14,508
Yes.

413
00:25:19,154 --> 00:25:21,731
After you got promoted
thanks to Ambassador Do,

414
00:25:22,296 --> 00:25:25,796
your mother seemed to step up
and take Do Hee's side completely.

415
00:25:26,495 --> 00:25:27,715
It seems that way.

416
00:25:29,029 --> 00:25:30,819
- Uncle.
- What?

417
00:25:30,821 --> 00:25:33,573
I could've earned that promotion
without Ambassador Do, you know.

418
00:25:33,821 --> 00:25:36,404
I worked hard to prove
I deserved that position.

419
00:25:37,113 --> 00:25:38,194
No one said otherwise.

420
00:25:38,196 --> 00:25:39,988
You said I owe it to Ambassador Do.

421
00:25:40,238 --> 00:25:41,863
Hearing that from you too...

422
00:25:41,904 --> 00:25:43,152
is really hard for me.

423
00:25:43,154 --> 00:25:45,152
Okay. I'm sorry.

424
00:25:45,154 --> 00:25:47,736
My mind's a mess right now.

425
00:25:47,738 --> 00:25:48,920
Why? What's going on?

426
00:25:51,120 --> 00:25:52,751
Ji Ni's mother...

427
00:25:53,071 --> 00:25:54,704
and the woman I've been seeing...

428
00:25:56,029 --> 00:25:57,238
Never mind.

429
00:25:57,895 --> 00:25:59,857
What did you come here to say?

430
00:26:01,779 --> 00:26:03,093
Actually...

431
00:26:04,120 --> 00:26:05,578
I can't say.

432
00:26:06,529 --> 00:26:08,444
Are you really going to marry
that grandma?

433
00:26:08,446 --> 00:26:09,604
Have you made up your mind?

434
00:26:10,863 --> 00:26:11,863
Hey!

435
00:26:13,835 --> 00:26:15,902
- It'd be my first marriage.
- That's exactly the problem.

436
00:26:15,904 --> 00:26:18,659
If you're all against it, I'll move out.

437
00:26:18,662 --> 00:26:20,733
Why seek anyone's approval at my age?

438
00:26:21,238 --> 00:26:25,321
I won't bend for anyone.

439
00:26:26,204 --> 00:26:27,595
Then what are you worried about?

440
00:26:30,688 --> 00:26:31,695
Okay.

441
00:26:31,988 --> 00:26:33,497
I'll tell you. Listen carefully.

442
00:26:35,029 --> 00:26:37,776
The child Ji Ni donated marrow to...

443
00:26:38,170 --> 00:26:41,944
is from her father's first family,
the one with his official wife...

444
00:26:41,946 --> 00:26:42,946
I know.

445
00:26:48,305 --> 00:26:49,858
The woman I'm seeing...

446
00:26:50,812 --> 00:26:52,807
is Ji Ni's father's official wife.

447
00:26:53,446 --> 00:26:54,446
What?

448
00:27:14,613 --> 00:27:17,819
(Family Register)

449
00:27:17,821 --> 00:27:19,944
I checked at the police station.
I'm on my way back now.

450
00:27:19,946 --> 00:27:21,194
See? I told you it wasn't her.

451
00:27:21,196 --> 00:27:22,819
I can't believe it.

452
00:27:22,821 --> 00:27:24,777
I'm sorry. Forgive Tae O too.

453
00:27:24,779 --> 00:27:26,111
Don't ever suspect me again.

454
00:27:26,113 --> 00:27:28,402
Say you're sorry. On your knees!

455
00:27:28,404 --> 00:27:30,861
- Then you apologize too.
- You're a mistress's daughter.

456
00:27:30,863 --> 00:27:33,320
- Mom?
- If someone has feelings for your mother,

457
00:27:33,322 --> 00:27:34,736
that's a good thing. What's the problem?

458
00:27:34,738 --> 00:27:36,611
I think you're the strange one.

459
00:27:36,613 --> 00:27:38,611
She was the woman you went
to the beach with, right?

460
00:27:38,613 --> 00:27:40,871
I heard she was a married man's mistress
until he passed away.

461
00:27:40,879 --> 00:27:43,194
- Dad may fire Ji Ni.
- How does that make any sense?

462
00:27:43,196 --> 00:27:45,027
Why should she be fired
for her parents' past?

463
00:27:45,029 --> 00:27:46,821
That's how our society works.

464
00:27:49,037 --> 00:27:51,037
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
